<p>
  A <a href="https://github.com/basecamp/lexxy">Lexxy</a> editor synced with
  <a href="https://github.com/jpcamara/lexxy-realtime">lexxy-realtime</a>.
  Lexical stores its content in the Yjs document as nested
  <code>Y.XmlText</code> nodes. Each room
  has a <code>Note</code> record, which <code>NoteChannel</code> creates when
  the first person joins. Your browser gets a signed token for this room's
  <code>body</code> field, and the channel rejects any other token.
</p>
<p>
  After each update, the server renders the note's whole body to HTML with
  <code>Y::Lexxy</code> and saves it to <code>body</code>, a plain text column.
  yrby's tests check that this HTML matches what a live Lexxy editor produces.
  The panel below loads the column over HTTP, so you can watch the saved HTML
  change as you type.
</p>
